          "date": "2026-11-12 04:03:38.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20711 tcu: add Trash Can audit feature",
        "message": "LU-20711 tcu: add Trash Can audit feature\n\nTo support the Trash Can audit feature, this patch does the\nfollowing changes:\n- Add a new MDT tunable \"mdd.*.trash_can_audit\" to control\n  recording of the audit information on the server side, disabled\n  by default.\n- Add a new flag URM_FL_AUDIT and set it when audit feature is\n  enabled, add unrm xattr extension struct unrm_audit to collect\n  audit information, including the deleter's UID, GID, NID and\n  JobID, also the original FID.\n- Add a new flag URM_FL_FULLPATH and unrm xattr extension struct\n  unrm_fullpath for future use.\n- Read unrm xattr with lgetxattr() instead of opening the object,\n  so that a symlink or a FIFO in the Trash Can can be purged too.\n- Report the error and stop ltrash purging if an audit record cannot\n  be written, instead of silently dropping the records.\n- Correct the logic in mdd_trash_declare_unrm_xattr_set(): Always\n  mark the object with LUSTRE_UNRM_FL; As long as audit is enabled,\n  set unrm_xattr and export audit information; If audit is disabled\n  and keep_ugpid is true, don't set unrm_xattr and audit information,\n  otherwise, only set unrm_xattr.\n\nLustre-change: https://review.whamcloud.com/68886\nLustre-commit: f1ac524305a2307be73c2f5bd7e262da89f2dedb\n\nFixes: 72920861c3b2 (\"LU-20006 tcu: keep FS flags unchanged after restore from Trash\")\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=119\nSigned-off-by: Emoly Liu <emoly@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I8db07948719f6791f1d1cb9030d5603963a6345e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
